# The image inspector runs this project's own check command in.
#
# Every project inspector judges commits one of these at its repository
# root, under exactly this name, and inspector builds it at check time and
# runs `script/check` inside the result (issue #47, see
# notes/20261025-project-image-from-committed-dockerfile.md). It is also
# meant to be the base of the box the work is written in, so what a check
# runs against cannot differ from what the work was built against.
#
# cimg/go:1.22, not golang:1.22, because script/check needs more than a Go
# toolchain: gcc and CGO_ENABLED=1 for `go test -race`, plus every shell
# tool .github/scripts/required-tools.sh names - `jq` among them, which
# golang:1.22 does not carry and which is a real runtime dependency of the
# shipped inspector-gate script, not only of its tests. A replacement base
# has to carry that whole list already: the check container has no
# network, so nothing can be installed while the check runs.
#
# Nothing is installed here because there is nothing to install - this
# project's Go module has no external dependencies at all (see go.mod).
# A project that does have them installs them here, at build time, where
# the network is still available.
FROM cimg/go:1.22
